Quick open (no server)
- Double-click index.html to open in your browser.

Run a local web server (recommended)
# Python 3 (PowerShell)
py -3 -m http.server 8000
# or
python -m http.server 8000

# Node (if Node.js installed)
npx http-server -p 8000

# VS Code Live Server (GUI)
# Install Live Server extension, open the folder, right-click index.html → Open with Live Server

Make the resume text-searchable (OCR)
1) Verify Python:
py -3 --version

2) Install Tesseract (choose one):
# With Chocolatey (if installed)
choco install tesseract -y
# Or download & install Tesseract manually from an official installer

3) Install OCRmyPDF (Python):
py -3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
py -3 -m pip install ocrmypdf

4) Run OCR to create a searchable PDF:
py -3 -m ocrmypdf "Srinath_M_Resume.pdf" "Srinath_M_Resume_searchable.pdf"

5) Replace the project file (optional):
Move-Item -LiteralPath "Srinath_M_Resume_searchable.pdf" -Destination "Srinath_M_Resume.pdf" -Force

Quick checks
Get-Item .\Srinath_M_Resume.pdf | Format-List Name,Length

# If pdftotext installed, extract text and search:
pdftotext Srinath_M_Resume.pdf - | Select-String -Pattern "SRINATH"

To stop a running Python server: press Ctrl+C in the PowerShell window.